## Routed findings and fixes

- F240 [Blocker], FIX at `d31c2431f`. Cause: `sentencePieces` joined only a punctuation
  run with no whitespace after it, so a comma before a space stayed its own flex item and
  the row gap opened a space before it. Shipped w05 page 8, w06 pages 3 and 6, and w07
  page 6 read "TAP , TAP , TAP!". Fix: the word-end punctuation run joins its word even
  when a space follows, and the space stays a plain piece. The tap-button count does not
  change, and no character moves or doubles. The pin flips from `it.fails` to `it` with its
  assertion unchanged. `phase3-decodable-punct.test.tsx` (F151) still passes.
- F242 [Major], FIX at `3dbd4fa9b`. Cause: the week page built all three tiles while
  `song` stays optional, so `?part=song` on a week without a song rendered an empty
  section with no control. Fix: a tile exists only for a part the week has, and a part
  screen without its content shows the link back to the week tiles. Shipped weeks keep
  three tiles. `phase3-reader-end.test.tsx` (F149) still passes.
- F241 [Nit], FIX at `0d2df682d`. Cause: a `play()` rejection before the queued
  `loadedmetadata` event ran the F147 clear first, and the queued arm then armed a stop for
  playback that never starts. Fix: `seekAndRun` returns a cancel for its queued `onReady`,
  and `reader.tsx` and `decodable.tsx` run it from their clear functions.
- Gate-blocking test typing, FIX at `5bda02bb0`. The round 2 song-lines test read a lyric
  item as `Element`, so `tsc --noEmit` failed with TS2345. The query now names
  `HTMLElement`. No assertion changed.

## Fail-first

The three pins ran as plain `it` on base `b38468630`, before any fix, in one heavy-run job.
The run exited 1 with 3 failed tests, each on its own assertion:

- F240: `expected 'TAP' to be 'TAP,'`.
- F241: `expected 1 to be +0`.
- F242: `expected null not to be null`.

The `it.fails` markers were restored before the fixes. `adversarial-f53c218e4.json` records
the same three failures.

